            "review_text": "Darryl C\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam84 contributions\n1\nAway from the propaganda\nSep 2017 • Solo\nI was looking for a quiet place, not packed to the gills with people and loud music, offering food and drink at reasonable prices near the reunification palace. I didn't hold out much hope. I chanced upon Ghem as I wandered down Pasteur St. A lovely spot. I only had a light lunch of salad but the menu looked good, the drinks menu interesting (I had quamquat and Tamarind) and the atmosphere quiet and inviting. I enjoyed my salad in peace.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 8, 2017",
